---
import ArticleShell from '../../components/ArticleShell.astro';
import { claim, articleFacts, andList } from '../../lib/articles.js';
import { withArticle } from '../../lib/grammar.js';
import { STAGES } from '../../lib/hue.js';

/**
 * Artikel: gezonde levensjaren. Het nieuws in de data: twintig jaar verschil tussen landen,
 * en een sprong in het Europese cijfer waarvan de data niet zegt waar hij vandaan komt.
 */
const { idx, h, g, y, lastStep, biggestBefore, flagged, first, source, fmt } = articleFacts('healthy-years');
const W = (name: string) => withArticle(name);
const Cap = (s: string) => s.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + s.slice(1);
const biggestRise = y.rows.at(-1);
const womenMore = g.womenAbove.length;

// Zinnen die niet uit één getal volgen; zie claim() in src/lib/articles.js.
claim(lastStep.change > 0 && (!biggestBefore || lastStep.change > Math.abs(biggestBefore.change)), 'A jump in the European figure: the largest one-year move');

const title = `A newborn in ${W(h.latest.name)} can expect ${fmt(h.gap)} more healthy years than in ${W(h.earliest.name)}`;
const description =
  `Healthy life years at birth range from ${fmt(h.earliest.total)} in ${W(h.earliest.name)} to ${fmt(h.latest.total)} in ${W(h.latest.name)} (${h.year}). ` +
  `The EU figure jumped to ${fmt(h.eu.total)}; the data does not say why.`;
---

<ArticleShell
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/notes/healthy-life-years-europe-gap/"
  hue={STAGES.healthy}
  published="2026-11-21"
  metricPath="/healthy-years/"
  metricLabel="Healthy years"
  cta="See the healthy life years in every country"
  source={source}
>
  <p slot="lead">
    A child born in {W(h.latest.name)} in {h.year} can expect <b>{fmt(h.latest.total)}</b> years without a
    health problem that limits daily life, according to Eurostat. In {W(h.earliest.name)} it is
    {' '}<b>{fmt(h.earliest.total)}</b>. That is {fmt(h.gap)} years of difference inside one continent.
  </p>

  <h2>A jump in the European figure</h2>
  <p>
    Across the European Union the figure was {fmt(h.eu.total)} years in {h.year}, against {fmt(y.euPrev)} a year
    earlier. A rise of {fmt(lastStep.change)} years in twelve months is the largest one-year move in the
    European series since it began in {first}{biggestBefore && <>; the largest before it was {fmt(Math.abs(biggestBefore.change))} years, from {biggestBefore.from} to {biggestBefore.to}</>}.
  </p>
  <p>
    It went up in {y.up.length} of the {y.rows.length} countries with a comparable figure and down in {y.down.length}.
    The biggest rise was in {W(biggestRise.name)}: from {fmt(biggestRise.series[y.prev])} to {fmt(biggestRise.total)}.
  </p>
  <div class="limits">
    <p>
      The data does not say why the European figure jumped. Healthy life years come from a survey
      question in which people say whether a health problem limits them, so a change can come from
      health, from how people answer, or from the survey itself.
      {flagged.length > 0 && <> Eurostat flags a break in {h.year} for {flagged.length}{' '}{flagged.length === 1 ? 'country' : 'countries'} ({andList(flagged.map((c: any) => W(c.name)))}), which are left out of the count above.</>}
      {' '}A single year is not a trend, and this note does not call it one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>{womenMore > g.womenLower ? "In most countries, women can expect more healthy years" : "In most countries, men can expect more healthy years"}</h2>
  <p>
    In {womenMore} of the {g.of} countries women can expect more healthy years than men. In {g.womenLower} it
    is the other way round; the widest gap in that direction is in {W(g.widest.name)}, at {fmt(g.widestGap)} years.
  </p>

  <h2>What this figure is, and what it is not</h2>
  <p>
    Healthy life years are an expectation for a newborn, calculated from today's health and death rates
    at every age. They are not the age at which someone alive today will become ill. And they rest on
    what people report about themselves.
  </p>
</ArticleShell>
